			<attacks>
				<description><![CDATA[Force Strike. Ranged Weapon Attack: +4 to hit, range 30 ft., one target you can see. Hit: 1d4 + 2 force damage.

If you attack with a double-bladed scimitar as part of the Attack action on your turn, you can use a bonus action immediately after to make a melee attack with it. This attack deals 1d4 slashing damage on a hit, instead of 2d4.]]></description>
				<attack identifier="59913619-6eb9-488c-bfe3-d0ce937ea15a" name="Ruidium Shortsword" range="5 ft" attack="+8 vs AC" damage="1d6+4 piercing" displayed="true" ability="Dexterity">
					<description><![CDATA[Finesse, Light]]></description>
				</attack>
				<attack identifier="961ac917-048c-429f-af6b-e17f1828f355" name="Double-Bladed Scimitar" range="5 ft" attack="+6 vs AC" damage="2d4+2 slashing" displayed="true" ability="Constitution">
					<description><![CDATA[Special (Double-Bladed Scimitar), Two-Handed]]></description>
				</attack>
				<attack identifier="8b4362d9-ed27-4086-92ca-59dfc641f080" name="Pepperbox" range="150/600" attack="+4 vs AC" damage="1d10+4 piercing" displayed="true" ability="Dexterity">
					<description><![CDATA[Misfire 2, Reload 6]]></description>
				</attack>
				<attack identifier="eb718c73-050f-4fd6-98fa-fe06b5909cc9" name="Dagger" range="20/60" attack="+8 vs AC" damage="1d4+4 piercing" displayed="true" ability="Dexterity">
					<description><![CDATA[Finesse, Light, Thrown]]></description>
				</attack>
			</attacks>
			<backstory><![CDATA[Before you became an adventurer, your life was already full of conflict and excitement, because you made a living tracking down people for pay. Unlike some people who collect bounties, though, you aren’t a savage who follows quarry into or through the wilderness. You’re involved in a lucrative trade, in the place where you live, that routinely tests your skills and survival instincts. What’s more, you aren’t alone, as a bounty hunter in the wild would be: you routinely interact with both the criminal subculture and other bounty hunters, maintaining contacts in both areas to help you succeed.

You might be a cunning thief-catcher, prowling the rooftops to catch one of the myriad burglars of the city. Perhaps you are someone who has your ear to the street, aware of the doings of thieves’ guilds and street gangs. You might be a "velvet mask" bounty hunter, one who blends in with high society and noble circles in order to catch the criminals that prey on the rich, whether pickpockets or con artists. The community where you plied your trade might have been one of Faerûn’s great metropolises, such as Waterdeep or Baldur’s Gate, or a less populous location, perhaps Luskan or Yartar-any place that’s large enough to have a steady supply of potential quarries.

As a member of an adventuring party, you might find it more difficult to pursue a personal agenda that doesn’t fit with the group’s objectives- but on the other hand, you can take down much more formidable targets with the help of your companions.


---

Despite his undeniable talent, Asmediseus struggled to find his place among his peers, often falling short of the lofty expectations set by his instructors. Frustration gnawed at his spirit as he toiled tirelessly to master the arcane arts of artifice, his efforts yielding only meagre results.
-
As a side job, I started interacting with the LOCAL CRIMINAL GUILD IN ZADASH. Being a rarer race, the richer people tend to act as if I  was some kind of attraction, allowing me to infiltrate high society parties and access targets others can't.

My methods are as diverse as the criminals I pursued. Some days, I donned the guise of a velvet-masked socialite, seamlessly blending into high society to ensnare those who preyed upon the wealthy and influential. Other times, I prowled the rooftops, my ear attuned to the whispers of thieves' guilds and street gangs, gathering information and unraveling the intricate web of criminal intrigue. 

It was during a fateful experiment gone awry that my destiny took an unexpected turn. In my fervent pursuit of knowledge, I stumbled upon a long-forgotten tome hidden within the school's vast library, its pages brimming with ancient secrets of clockwork magic. Ignoring the warnings of caution, I delved deep into the arcane mysteries contained within, eager to unlock the power that lay dormant within my grasp.

As I conducted my research, I unwittingly awakened a latent spark of magic that lay dormant within my soul, a fusion of mechanical ingenuity and mystical energy. The arcane energies surged through my veins, suffusing my being with the essence of Mechanus, the plane of order.

With my newfound power, I created my companion Cycyd, and later, my protector Vangyrd.
-

Traditional artificial magic doesn't resonate with me, so I double dip, combining alchemical and clockwork tools and trinkets with some innate magic I have gained along the way. I also have access to some fey magic, but I'm not sure how to channel it yet.

Port Damali, From Marqet
Landed on the menagerie coast moved to Zadash to go to school, met Sarovan, travelled with him]]></backstory>
			<background-trinket>A small symbol of The Burrow</background-trinket>
			<background-traits>I always have a plan for what to do when things go wrong.
I am incredibly slow to trust. Those who seem the fairest often have the most to hide.</background-traits>
			<background-ideals>People. I’m loyal to my friends, not to any ideals, and everyone else can take a trip down the Styx for all I care. (Neutral)</background-ideals>
			<background-bonds>I’m guilty of a terrible crime. I hope I can redeem myself for it.</background-bonds>
			<background-flaws>I turn tail and run when things look bad.</background-flaws>
			<background>
				<feature name="Feature: Ear to the Ground">
					<description><![CDATA[You are in frequent contact with people in the segment of society that your chosen quarries move through. These people might be associated with the criminal underworld, the rough-and-tumble folk of the streets, or members of high society. This connection comes in the form of a contact in any city you visit, a person who provides information about the people and places of the local area.]]></description>
				</feature>
			</background>
